1. How to Create EBS Volumes in AWS

EBS (Elastic Block Store) provides extra storage for an EC2 instance.

Steps to Create an EBS Volume
Go to AWS Console → EC2 → Elastic Block Store → Volumes.
Click Create volume.
Select the volume type, for example:
gp3

Enter the required size.

Example:

10 GB
12 GB
14 GB

Select the Availability Zone.

Important: The EBS volume and EC2 instance must be in the same Availability Zone.

Example:

EC2 → ap-south-1b
EBS → ap-south-1b
Click Create volume.

Repeat the same steps if you need multiple volumes.

2. Attach the EBS Volume to EC2

After creating the volume:

EC2 → Volumes
→ Select the volume
→ Actions
→ Attach volume
→ Select your EC2 instance
→ Attach

After attaching the volume, connect to the EC2 instance and check:

lsblk

The new EBS disk should appear in the output.

Example
EC2 Instance
    |
    ├── EBS 10 GB
    ├── EBS 12 GB
    └── EBS 14 GB

